randint - Generates random integer within
boundary inclusive of both values.
random - Generates random float from 0 inclusive
to 1 not inclusive. Can be manipulated with
multiplication
Modules are parts of a complete program and 
users may make their own modules.

append - adds an item to the last value of a list
insert - list.insert(index, value) right after index
specified
remove - list.remove(value) specified value. Returns
ValueError if value is not found in list.
pop - list.pop(index) Removes specified index in a list.
If no index is specified, removes last item in list.

list within a list can be made by
list1 = [value1, value2, value3, value4]
list2 = [value5, value6]

list = [list1, list2]
output: list = [[value1, value2, value3, value4],[value5, value6]]

To pull item from a nested list grid, do this
list[i1][i2] where i1 is row (horizontal) and i2 is column (vertical)